          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold font-heading text-ink-deep">
            What is missing from legacy tools
          </h2>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate mt-1">
            Contractors frequently share these recurring complaints in trade forums regarding answering tools.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-paper border border-sky-blue">
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-base text-ink-deep mb-2">Nobody Owns the Result</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate leading-relaxed">
              Software vendors sell per-minute bundles or software access, but when a call drops or an address is booked incorrectly, there is no one accountable for tuning the system.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-paper border border-sky-blue">
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-base text-ink-deep mb-2">Wrong Bookings & Technical Errors</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate leading-relaxed">
              Generic bots schedule appointments in the middle of travel routes or book water restoration extractions when crews only handle HVAC diagnostics.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-paper border border-sky-blue">
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-base text-ink-deep mb-2">Surprise Bills & Per-Minute Hikes</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate leading-relaxed">
              Complicated overage formulas and sudden burst penalties when severe weather strikes make monthly bills unpredictable.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-paper border border-sky-blue">
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-base text-ink-deep mb-2">Weak Escalation Handoffs</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate leading-relaxed">
              When a desperate homeowner needs an immediate emergency crew, automated tools often loop or deliver dead silence instead of dialing on-call staff.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-paper border border-sky-blue">
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-base text-ink-deep mb-2">Annual Contract Lock-in</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate leading-relaxed">
              Enterprise platforms force trades companies into expensive 12-month commitments before proving performance on real customer calls.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-paper border border-sky-blue">
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-base text-ink-deep mb-2">Data & Number Hostage</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate leading-relaxed">
              Many services hold onto the telephone numbers or refuse clean data exports when a contractor decides to take their dispatch in-house.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
